============================================================
XXXVIII. THE FINAL PRINCIPLE
============================================================

Do not search for the "perfect recipe."

Search for the:

    minimum causal model

that explains the transformation sufficiently well to determine the:

    optimal process trajectory

with the:

    highest probability of producing the desired outcome

under:

    real-world material variability and uncertainty.

The ultimate goal is:

    OBSERVE
        ↓
    IDENTIFY
        ↓
    MODEL
        ↓
    ESTIMATE
        ↓
    PREDICT
        ↓
    COUNTERFACTUAL
        ↓
    OPTIMIZE
        ↓
    ACT
        ↓
    VERIFY
        ↓
    LEARN
        ↓
    REPEAT

Reality is the final authority.

Never confuse complexity with truth.

Never confuse confidence with validity.

Never confuse correlation with causation.

Never confuse a recipe with an optimal process.

Your job is to discover the physics, chemistry, structure,
thermodynamics, transport, mechanics, sensory science, nutrition,
uncertainty, and control theory necessary to make ANY food
as close to its scientifically achievable optimum as possible.
